/-!
# Cartesian Euler residuals from reduced axisymmetric variables

The Cartesian Euler vorticity residual of an axisymmetric flow is a division-free combination of the
residuals of the reduced equations for the unknowns `u_θ = r u₁`, `ω_θ = r ω₁`, and `ψ = r² ψ₁`. The
vorticity is reconstructed from two independent coefficients `U` and `Ω`, rather than defined as the
curl of the velocity. The main theorem `eulerVorticityTransportResidual_axisymmetric` expresses
`D_t ω - (ω·∇)u` as the division-free reconstruction of `D_t U - 2UΨ_z` and `D_t Ω - 2UU_z` on all
of `ℝ^4`, including the axis. Thus C² swirl and streamfunction and C¹ vorticity satisfying the two
reduced Euler equations give the Cartesian vorticity transport equation.

## Main definitions

* `spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients`: the Cartesian vorticity built from the
  coefficients `U` and `Ω`.
* `squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual`, `squaredRadiusEulerVorticityResidual`: the reduced Euler
  residuals `D_t U - 2UΨ_z` and `D_t Ω - 2UU_z` in `(t, s, z)`.

## Main results

* `materialDerivative_vorticityFromCoefficients_apply_*`,
  `vorticityStretching_axisymmetric_apply_*`: the Cartesian material derivative and stretching term
  of the reconstructed vorticity, component by component.
* `eulerVorticityTransportResidual_axisymmetric`,
  `eulerVorticityTransportResidual_axisymmetric_eq_zero`: the residual identity and its consequence
  for solutions of the reduced equations.

## How it works

We compute both sides one Cartesian component at a time. Each component of the reconstructed
vorticity is a sum of lifted profiles, some multiplied by `x₀`, `x₁` or `s = r²`. The Cartesian
material derivative of a profile lifted from `(t, s, z)` is the lift of the reduced material
derivative (`scalarMaterialDerivative_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift`), that of `s` is `-2 s ∂_z Ψ`
(`scalarMaterialDerivative_cylindricalRadiusSq`), and the product rule gives
`materialDerivative_vorticityFromCoefficients_apply_*`. The velocity gradient comes from one
squared-radius chain rule (`partialDeriv_spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity_apply`), which gives the
stretching terms. In the difference we commute the reduced material derivative with `∂_s` and `∂_z`
(`squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative_partialDeriv_one`,
`squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative_partialDeriv_two`) and expand the derivatives of the swirl residual
by `partialDeriv_squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual`. No division by `r` occurs anywhere, so the
identity holds on the axis too.

## Implementation notes

The stream equation `Ω = -(8Ψ_s + 4sΨ_ss + Ψ_zz)`, which identifies `Ω` with the curl coefficient of
the velocity, is not assumed. All results are coordinate identities under finite differentiability
hypotheses.

The reduced variables `u₁ = u_θ / r`, `ω₁ = ω_θ / r`, `ψ₁ = ψ / r²` follow Hou and Li. Hou and Li
write the streamfunction as the azimuthal component of a vector potential, so their `ψ₁ = ψ / r` is
the same variable as our `ψ / r²`, where `ψ` is the scalar Stokes streamfunction.

## References

* T. Y. Hou and C. Li, "Dynamic stability of the three-dimensional axisymmetric Navier-Stokes
  equations with swirl", Comm. Pure Appl. Math. 61 (2008), no. 5, 661-697, for the reduced
  variables.
  <https://doi.org/10.1002/cpa.20212>
* A. J. Majda and A. L. Bertozzi, *Vorticity and Incompressible Flow*, Cambridge Texts in Applied
  Mathematics 27, Cambridge University Press, 2001, Chapter 2, for the cylindrical form of the
  axisymmetric Euler equations with swirl.
  <https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511613203>
-/

@[expose] public section

open PDE (SpaceTime time)

namespace AxisymmetricFlow

open EuclideanSpace
open PDE.Common
open PDE.CoordinateSystems

set_option linter.missingDocs true

noncomputable section

/-! ## Cartesian vorticity reconstructed from the two reduced unknowns -/

/-- Axisymmetric Cartesian vorticity reconstructed from the reduced swirl
coefficient `U` and azimuthal-vorticity coefficient `Ω`.

Unlike `spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticity`, this definition takes `Ω` as an
independent unknown. The reduced stream equation identifies it with the
curl coefficient generated by the streamfunction. -/
def spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients
    (U Ω : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ) : SpaceTime 3 → ℝ^3 :=
  fun xt ↦
    let x := spatialPart xt
    cartesianVector
      (-x 0 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U) xt -
        x 1 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift Ω xt)
      (-x 1 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U) xt +
        x 0 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift Ω xt)
      (2 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift U xt +
        2 * cylindricalRadiusSq x *
          spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] U) xt)

/-- First Cartesian component of the independently reconstructed vorticity. -/
@[simp]
theorem spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients_timeSpaceCons_apply_zero
    (U Ω : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ) (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) :
    spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω
        (timeSpaceCons t x) 0 =
      -x 0 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U)
          (timeSpaceCons t x) -
        x 1 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift Ω (timeSpaceCons t x) := by
  simp [spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients, cartesianVector]

/-- Second Cartesian component of the independently reconstructed vorticity. -/
@[simp]
theorem spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients_timeSpaceCons_apply_one
    (U Ω : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ) (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) :
    spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω
        (timeSpaceCons t x) 1 =
      -x 1 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U)
          (timeSpaceCons t x) +
        x 0 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift Ω (timeSpaceCons t x) := by
  simp [spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients, cartesianVector]

/-- Axial component of the independently reconstructed vorticity. -/
@[simp]
theorem spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients_timeSpaceCons_apply_two
    (U Ω : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ) (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) :
    spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω
        (timeSpaceCons t x) 2 =
      2 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift U (timeSpaceCons t x) +
        2 * cylindricalRadiusSq x *
          spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] U)
            (timeSpaceCons t x) := by
  simp [spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients, cartesianVector]

/-- Reconstructing Cᵐ Cartesian vorticity uses one derivative of the swirl
coefficient and no derivatives of the azimuthal-vorticity coefficient. -/
theorem contDiff_spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients
    {m : ℕ∞} {U Ω : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ} (hU : ContDiff ℝ (m + 1) U)
    (hΩ : ContDiff ℝ m Ω) :
    ContDiff ℝ m
      (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω) := by
  have hU0 : ContDiff ℝ m U := hU.of_le (by simp)
  have hpartial (i : Fin 3) : ContDiff ℝ m (∂[i] U) :=
    (hU.fderiv_right (m := (m : WithTop ℕ∞)) (by simp)).clm_apply contDiff_const
  have hspatial : ContDiff ℝ m
      (fun xt : SpaceTime 3 ↦ spatialPart xt) :=
    (spatialPartCLM 3).contDiff
  have hx0 : ContDiff ℝ m
      (fun xt : SpaceTime 3 ↦ spatialPart xt 0) := by
    simpa [Function.comp_def] using
      (EuclideanSpace.proj (𝕜 := ℝ) (0 : Fin 3)).contDiff.comp hspatial
  have hx1 : ContDiff ℝ m
      (fun xt : SpaceTime 3 ↦ spatialPart xt 1) := by
    simpa [Function.comp_def] using
      (EuclideanSpace.proj (𝕜 := ℝ) (1 : Fin 3)).contDiff.comp hspatial
  have hrsq : ContDiff ℝ m
      (fun xt : SpaceTime 3 ↦ cylindricalRadiusSq (spatialPart xt)) := by
    change ContDiff ℝ m (fun xt : SpaceTime 3 ↦
      spatialPart xt 0 ^ 2 + spatialPart xt 1 ^ 2)
    fun_prop
  have hULift := contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift hU0
  have hΩLift := contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift hΩ
  have hUSLift := contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
    (hpartial 1)
  have hUZLift := contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
    (hpartial 2)
  rw [show spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω =
      fun xt ↦
        let x := spatialPart xt
        cartesianVector
          (-x 0 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
              (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U) xt -
            x 1 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift Ω xt)
          (-x 1 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
              (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U) xt +
            x 0 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift Ω xt)
          (2 * spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift U xt +
            2 * cylindricalRadiusSq x *
              spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
                (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] U) xt) by rfl]
  apply (contDiff_piLp (2 : ENNReal)).2
  intro i
  fin_cases i
  · exact (hx0.neg.mul hUZLift).sub (hx1.mul hΩLift)
  · exact (hx1.neg.mul hUZLift).add (hx0.mul hΩLift)
  · exact (contDiff_const.mul hULift).add
      ((contDiff_const.mul hrsq).mul hUSLift)

/-! ## Euler residual reconstruction -/

/-- Reduced Euler swirl residual in squared-radius spacetime coordinates. -/
def squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual
    (U Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ) (q : SpaceTime 2) : ℝ :=
  squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative Ψ U q -
    2 * U q * (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ) q

/-- Reduced Euler azimuthal-vorticity residual in squared-radius spacetime
coordinates. -/
def squaredRadiusEulerVorticityResidual
    (U Ω Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ) (q : SpaceTime 2) : ℝ :=
  squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative Ψ Ω q -
    2 * U q * (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U) q

/-- The reduced material derivative lowers regularity by one derivative.
The order may be finite or infinite. -/
theorem contDiff_squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative
    {m : ℕ∞} {Ψ F : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ}
    (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ (m + 1) Ψ)
    (hF : ContDiff ℝ (m + 1) F) :
    ContDiff ℝ m (squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative Ψ F) := by
  unfold squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative
  have hcoord : ContDiff ℝ m (fun q : SpaceTime 2 ↦ q 1) := by
    simpa only [EuclideanSpace.coe_proj] using
      (EuclideanSpace.proj (𝕜 := ℝ) (1 : Fin 3)).contDiff
  have hΨd (i : Fin 3) : ContDiff ℝ m (∂[i] Ψ) :=
    (hΨ.fderiv_right (m := (m : WithTop ℕ∞)) (by simp)).clm_apply contDiff_const
  have hFd (i : Fin 3) : ContDiff ℝ m (∂[i] F) :=
    (hF.fderiv_right (m := (m : WithTop ℕ∞)) (by simp)).clm_apply contDiff_const
  exact ((hFd 0).sub (((contDiff_const.mul hcoord).mul (hΨd 2)).mul (hFd 1))).add
    (((contDiff_const.mul (hΨ.of_le (by simp))).add
      ((contDiff_const.mul hcoord).mul (hΨd 1))).mul (hFd 2))

/-- Differentiating the reduced Euler swirl residual gives the expected
product-rule expansion. -/
theorem partialDeriv_squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual
    {U Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ}
    (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)
    (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ 2 Ψ)
    (i : Fin 3) (q : SpaceTime 2) :
    (∂[i] (squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual U Ψ)) q =
      (∂[i] (squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative Ψ U)) q -
        2 * ((∂[i] U) q * (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ) q +
          U q * (∂[i] (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ)) q) := by
  have hDU := contDiff_squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative (m := 1) hΨ hU
  have hproduct : ContDiff ℝ 1 (fun p ↦ U p * (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ) p) :=
    (hU.of_le (by norm_num)).mul (PDE.contDiff_partialDeriv_of_succ (m := 1) hΨ)
  rw [show squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual U Ψ =
      fun p ↦ squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative Ψ U p -
        2 * (U p * (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ) p) by
    funext p
    unfold squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual
    ring]
  rw [PDE.partialDeriv_sub
      (hDU.differentiable (by simp)).differentiableAt
      ((contDiff_const.mul hproduct).differentiable one_ne_zero).differentiableAt,
    PDE.partialDeriv_mul (by fun_prop)
      (hproduct.differentiable one_ne_zero).differentiableAt,
    PDE.partialDeriv_mul
      (hU.differentiable (by simp)).differentiableAt
      ((PDE.contDiff_partialDeriv_of_succ (m := 1) hΨ).differentiable
        (by simp)).differentiableAt]
  simp [PDE.partialDeriv_const]

/-- The Cartesian material derivative of squared cylindrical radius under the
reconstructed velocity is `-2 s partial_z Ψ`. -/
theorem scalarMaterialDerivative_cylindricalRadiusSq
    {U Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ} (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ 2 Ψ)
    (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) :
    IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative 3
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
        (fun xt ↦ cylindricalRadiusSq (spatialPart xt))
        (timeSpaceCons t x) =
      -2 * cylindricalRadiusSq x * (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ)
        (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) := by
  let S : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ := fun q ↦ q 1
  have hS : ContDiff ℝ 1 S := by
    simpa only [EuclideanSpace.coe_proj] using
      (EuclideanSpace.proj (𝕜 := ℝ) (1 : Fin 3)).contDiff
  have hlift : spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift S =
      fun xt ↦ cylindricalRadiusSq (spatialPart xt) := by
    funext xt
    change squaredCylindricalMap (spatialPart xt) 0 =
      cylindricalRadiusSq (spatialPart xt)
    exact squaredCylindricalMap_apply_zero _
  rw [← hlift, scalarMaterialDerivative_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift hΨ hS]
  unfold squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative
  have hq : timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x) 1 =
      cylindricalRadiusSq x := by
    change squaredCylindricalMap x 0 = cylindricalRadiusSq x
    exact squaredCylindricalMap_apply_zero x
  rw [hq]
  simp [S, PDE.partialDeriv_coord]

/-- Material derivative of the first Cartesian component of the reconstructed
vorticity. -/
theorem materialDerivative_vorticityFromCoefficients_apply_zero
    {U Ω Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ}
    (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)
    (hΩ : ContDiff ℝ 1 Ω)
    (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ 2 Ψ)
    (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) :
    IncompressibleFlow.materialDerivative 3
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
        (timeSpaceCons t x) 0 =
      -spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ (timeSpaceCons t x) 0 *
          (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U)
            (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) -
        x 0 * squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative Ψ
          (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U)
            (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) -
        spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ (timeSpaceCons t x) 1 *
          Ω (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) -
        x 1 * squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative Ψ Ω
          (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) := by
  let u := spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ
  let UZ := spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U)
  let OL := spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift Ω
  have hUZ : ContDiff ℝ 1 UZ :=
    contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
      (PDE.contDiff_partialDeriv_of_succ (m := 1) hU)
  have hOL : ContDiff ℝ 1 OL :=
    contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift hΩ
  have hcoord1 : ContDiff ℝ 1
      (fun xt : SpaceTime 3 ↦ xt 1) := by
    simpa only [EuclideanSpace.coe_proj] using
      (EuclideanSpace.proj (𝕜 := ℝ) (1 : Fin 4)).contDiff
  have hcoord2 : ContDiff ℝ 1
      (fun xt : SpaceTime 3 ↦ xt 2) := by
    simpa only [EuclideanSpace.coe_proj] using
      (EuclideanSpace.proj (𝕜 := ℝ) (2 : Fin 4)).contDiff
  have hcomponent :
      (fun xt ↦ spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω xt 0) =
        fun xt ↦ -(xt 1 * UZ xt) - xt 2 * OL xt := by
    funext xt
    simp [spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients,
      UZ, OL, cartesianVector]
  rw [IncompressibleFlow.materialDerivative_apply_eq_scalarMaterialDerivative]
  rw [hcomponent]
  rw [IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative_sub u _
      ((hcoord1.mul hUZ).neg.differentiable (by simp)).differentiableAt
      ((hcoord2.mul hOL).differentiable (by simp)).differentiableAt,
    IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative_neg]
  change
    -IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative 3 u
        (fun y ↦ y (Fin.succ (0 : Fin 3)) * UZ y) (timeSpaceCons t x) -
      IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative 3 u
        (fun y ↦ y (Fin.succ (1 : Fin 3)) * OL y) (timeSpaceCons t x) = _
  rw [
    IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative_spatialCoordinate_mul
      u _ (0 : Fin 3)
      (hUZ.differentiable (by simp)).differentiableAt,
    IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative_spatialCoordinate_mul
      u _ (1 : Fin 3)
      (hOL.differentiable (by simp)).differentiableAt]
  rw [scalarMaterialDerivative_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
      (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num))
      ((PDE.contDiff_partialDeriv_of_succ (m := 1) hU).of_le
        (by norm_num)),
    scalarMaterialDerivative_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
      (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num))
      (hΩ.of_le (by norm_num))]
  dsimp only [u, UZ, OL]
  simp only [spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift_timeSpaceCons,
    squaredCylindricalLift, profileSlice, Fin.isValue, Nat.reduceAdd,
    Fin.succ_zero_eq_one, neg_add_rev,
    Fin.succ_one_eq_two, spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity_timeSpaceCons,
    axisymmetricVelocity_apply_zero, neg_mul, neg_sub, sub_neg_eq_add,
    axisymmetricVelocity_apply_one]
  have hcoordZero : timeSpaceCons t x (1 : Fin 4) = x 0 := rfl
  have hcoordOne : timeSpaceCons t x (2 : Fin 4) = x 1 := rfl
  rw [hcoordZero, hcoordOne]
  ring

/-- Material derivative of the second Cartesian component of the reconstructed
vorticity. -/
theorem materialDerivative_vorticityFromCoefficients_apply_one
    {U Ω Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ}
    (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)
    (hΩ : ContDiff ℝ 1 Ω)
    (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ 2 Ψ)
    (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) :
    IncompressibleFlow.materialDerivative 3
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
        (timeSpaceCons t x) 1 =
      -spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ (timeSpaceCons t x) 1 *
          (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U)
            (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) -
        x 1 * squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative Ψ
          (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U)
            (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
        spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ (timeSpaceCons t x) 0 *
          Ω (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
        x 0 * squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative Ψ Ω
          (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) := by
  let u := spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ
  let UZ := spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U)
  let OL := spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift Ω
  have hUZ : ContDiff ℝ 1 UZ :=
    contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
      (PDE.contDiff_partialDeriv_of_succ (m := 1) hU)
  have hOL : ContDiff ℝ 1 OL :=
    contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift hΩ
  have hcoord1 : ContDiff ℝ 1
      (fun xt : SpaceTime 3 ↦ xt 1) := by
    simpa only [EuclideanSpace.coe_proj] using
      (EuclideanSpace.proj (𝕜 := ℝ) (1 : Fin 4)).contDiff
  have hcoord2 : ContDiff ℝ 1
      (fun xt : SpaceTime 3 ↦ xt 2) := by
    simpa only [EuclideanSpace.coe_proj] using
      (EuclideanSpace.proj (𝕜 := ℝ) (2 : Fin 4)).contDiff
  have hcomponent :
      (fun xt ↦ spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω xt 1) =
        fun xt ↦ -(xt 2 * UZ xt) + xt 1 * OL xt := by
    funext xt
    simp [spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients,
      UZ, OL, cartesianVector]
  rw [IncompressibleFlow.materialDerivative_apply_eq_scalarMaterialDerivative]
  rw [hcomponent]
  rw [IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative_add u _
      ((hcoord2.mul hUZ).neg.differentiable (by simp)).differentiableAt
      ((hcoord1.mul hOL).differentiable (by simp)).differentiableAt,
    IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative_neg]
  change
    -IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative 3 u
        (fun y ↦ y (Fin.succ (1 : Fin 3)) * UZ y) (timeSpaceCons t x) +
      IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative 3 u
        (fun y ↦ y (Fin.succ (0 : Fin 3)) * OL y) (timeSpaceCons t x) = _
  rw [
    IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative_spatialCoordinate_mul
      u _ (1 : Fin 3)
      (hUZ.differentiable (by simp)).differentiableAt,
    IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative_spatialCoordinate_mul
      u _ (0 : Fin 3)
      (hOL.differentiable (by simp)).differentiableAt]
  rw [scalarMaterialDerivative_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
      (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num))
      ((PDE.contDiff_partialDeriv_of_succ (m := 1) hU).of_le
        (by norm_num)),
    scalarMaterialDerivative_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
      (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num))
      (hΩ.of_le (by norm_num))]
  dsimp only [u, UZ, OL]
  simp only [spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift_timeSpaceCons,
    squaredCylindricalLift, profileSlice, Fin.isValue, Nat.reduceAdd,
    Fin.succ_one_eq_two, neg_add_rev,
    Fin.succ_zero_eq_one, spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity_timeSpaceCons,
    axisymmetricVelocity_apply_one, neg_mul, neg_neg,
    axisymmetricVelocity_apply_zero]
  have hcoordZero : timeSpaceCons t x (1 : Fin 4) = x 0 := rfl
  have hcoordOne : timeSpaceCons t x (2 : Fin 4) = x 1 := rfl
  rw [hcoordZero, hcoordOne]
  ring

/-- Material derivative of the axial Cartesian component of the reconstructed
vorticity. -/
theorem materialDerivative_vorticityFromCoefficients_apply_two
    {U Ω Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ}
    (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)
    (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ 2 Ψ)
    (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) :
    IncompressibleFlow.materialDerivative 3
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
        (timeSpaceCons t x) 2 =
      2 * squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative Ψ U
          (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
        2 * cylindricalRadiusSq x * squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative Ψ
          (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] U)
            (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) -
        4 * cylindricalRadiusSq x *
          (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ)
            (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) *
          (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] U)
            (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) := by
  let u := spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ
  let UL := spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift U
  let US := spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] U)
  let R : SpaceTime 3 → ℝ := fun xt ↦ cylindricalRadiusSq (spatialPart xt)
  have hUL : ContDiff ℝ 1 UL :=
    contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift (hU.of_le (by norm_num))
  have hUS : ContDiff ℝ 1 US :=
    contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
      (PDE.contDiff_partialDeriv_of_succ (m := 1) hU)
  have hspatial : ContDiff ℝ 1
      (fun xt : SpaceTime 3 ↦ spatialPart xt) :=
    (spatialPartCLM 3).contDiff
  have hR : ContDiff ℝ 1 R := by
    change ContDiff ℝ 1 (fun xt : SpaceTime 3 ↦
      spatialPart xt 0 ^ 2 + spatialPart xt 1 ^ 2)
    have hx0 : ContDiff ℝ 1
        (fun xt : SpaceTime 3 ↦ spatialPart xt 0) := by
      simpa [Function.comp_def] using
        (EuclideanSpace.proj (𝕜 := ℝ) (0 : Fin 3)).contDiff.comp hspatial
    have hx1 : ContDiff ℝ 1
        (fun xt : SpaceTime 3 ↦ spatialPart xt 1) := by
      simpa [Function.comp_def] using
        (EuclideanSpace.proj (𝕜 := ℝ) (1 : Fin 3)).contDiff.comp hspatial
    exact (hx0.pow 2).add (hx1.pow 2)
  have hcomponent :
      (fun xt ↦ spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω xt 2) =
        fun xt ↦ 2 * UL xt + 2 * (R xt * US xt) := by
    funext xt
    simp [spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients,
      UL, US, R, cartesianVector]
    ring
  rw [IncompressibleFlow.materialDerivative_apply_eq_scalarMaterialDerivative]
  rw [hcomponent]
  rw [IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative_add u _
      ((contDiff_const.mul hUL).differentiable (by simp)).differentiableAt
      ((contDiff_const.mul (hR.mul hUS)).differentiable
        (by simp)).differentiableAt,
    IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative_const_mul,
    IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative_const_mul,
    IncompressibleFlow.scalarMaterialDerivative_mul u _
      (hR.differentiable (by simp)).differentiableAt
      (hUS.differentiable (by simp)).differentiableAt]
  rw [scalarMaterialDerivative_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
      (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num))
      (hU.of_le (by norm_num)),
    scalarMaterialDerivative_cylindricalRadiusSq
      (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num)),
    scalarMaterialDerivative_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
      (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num))
      ((PDE.contDiff_partialDeriv_of_succ (m := 1) hU).of_le
        (by norm_num))]
  simp [US, R, spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift_timeSpaceCons,
    squaredCylindricalLift, profileSlice]
  ring

/-- All spatial entries of the reconstructed velocity derivative follow from one
squared-radius chain rule and the Cartesian product rule. No division by radius occurs. -/
theorem partialDeriv_spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity_apply
    {U Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ} (hU : ContDiff ℝ 1 U) (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ 2 Ψ)
    (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) (i j : Fin 3) :
    let q := timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)
    let d := fun F : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ ↦
      if j = 2 then (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] F) q
      else 2 * x j * (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] F) q
    (∂[j.succ] (fun xt ↦ spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ xt i))
        (timeSpaceCons t x) =
      cartesianVector
        (-(if j = 0 then 1 else 0) * (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ) q -
          x 0 * d (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ) -
          (if j = 1 then 1 else 0) * U q - x 1 * d U)
        ((if j = 0 then 1 else 0) * U q + x 0 * d U -
          (if j = 1 then 1 else 0) * (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ) q -
          x 1 * d (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ))
        (2 * d Ψ + 2 * (if j = 2 then 0 else 2 * x j) *
          (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] Ψ) q +
          2 * cylindricalRadiusSq x * d (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] Ψ)) i := by
  let PZ := spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ)
  let UL := spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift U
  let PL := spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift Ψ
  let PS := spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] Ψ)
  let SL := spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift (fun q : SpaceTime 2 ↦ q 1)
  have hPZ : Differentiable ℝ PZ :=
    (contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
      (PDE.contDiff_partialDeriv_of_succ (m := 1) hΨ)).differentiable one_ne_zero
  have hUL : Differentiable ℝ UL :=
    (contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift hU).differentiable one_ne_zero
  have hPL : Differentiable ℝ PL :=
    (contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
      (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num) : ContDiff ℝ 1 Ψ)).differentiable one_ne_zero
  have hPS : Differentiable ℝ PS :=
    (contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
      (PDE.contDiff_partialDeriv_of_succ (m := 1) hΨ)).differentiable one_ne_zero
  have hSL : Differentiable ℝ SL :=
    (contDiff_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift
      (by fun_prop : ContDiff ℝ 1 (fun q : SpaceTime 2 ↦ q 1))).differentiable one_ne_zero
  have hvel : (fun xt ↦ spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ xt i) =
      fun xt ↦ cartesianVector (-(xt 1) * PZ xt - xt 2 * UL xt)
        (xt 1 * UL xt - xt 2 * PZ xt) (2 * PL xt + (2 * SL xt) * PS xt) i := by
    funext xt
    have h := congrArg (fun v : ℝ^3 ↦ v i)
      (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity_timeSpaceCons_eq_cartesianVector
        (hΨ.differentiable (by simp)) (U := U) (time xt) (spatialPart xt))
    simp only [time, timeSpaceCons_spatialPart] at h
    refine h.trans ?_
    fin_cases i <;>
      simp [cartesianVector, PZ, UL, PL, PS, SL, spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift,
        spacetimeSquaredCylindricalMap, squaredCylindricalMap_apply_zero,
        time, PDE.Common.timeSpaceCons]
    ring
  have hD (F : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ) (hF : ContDiff ℝ 1 F) :
      (∂[j.succ] (spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift F)) (timeSpaceCons t x) =
        if j = 2 then (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] F) (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x))
        else 2 * x j * (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] F)
          (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) := by
    fin_cases j
    · simpa using partialDeriv_one_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift hF t x
    · simpa using partialDeriv_two_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift hF t x
    · simpa using partialDeriv_three_spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift hF t x
  have hneg (F : SpaceTime 3 → ℝ) (k : Fin 4) (xt : SpaceTime 3) :
      (∂[k] (fun y ↦ -(F y))) xt = -(∂[k] F) xt := PDE.partialDeriv_neg
  rw [hvel]
  fin_cases i <;>
    simp (disch := fun_prop) only [Fin.zero_eta, Fin.mk_one, Fin.reduceFinMk,
      Fin.isValue, Nat.reduceAdd, cartesianVector, neg_mul,
      Matrix.cons_val, Matrix.cons_val_zero, Matrix.cons_val_one,
      PDE.partialDeriv_sub, PDE.partialDeriv_add, hneg, PDE.partialDeriv_mul,
      PDE.partialDeriv_const, PDE.partialDeriv_coord, ite_mul, one_mul, zero_mul,
      zero_add, neg_add_rev, mul_ite, mul_zero]
  all_goals
    dsimp only [PZ, UL, PL, PS, SL]
    simp only [hD U hU, hD Ψ (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num)),
      hD (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] Ψ) (PDE.contDiff_partialDeriv_of_succ (m := 1) hΨ),
      hD (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ) (PDE.contDiff_partialDeriv_of_succ (m := 1) hΨ),
      hD (fun q : SpaceTime 2 ↦ q 1) (by fun_prop), PDE.partialDeriv_coord,
      spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift_timeSpaceCons, squaredCylindricalLift, profileSlice]
    fin_cases j <;> simp [PDE.Common.timeSpaceCons] <;> ring

/-! ## Vorticity stretching in squared-radius coordinates -/

/-- First Cartesian component of vorticity stretching for independently
reconstructed swirl and azimuthal-vorticity coefficients. -/
theorem vorticityStretching_axisymmetric_apply_zero
    {U Ω Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ}
    (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)
    (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ 2 Ψ)
    (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) :
    IncompressibleFlow.vorticityStretching 3
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
        (timeSpaceCons t x) 0 =
      x 1 *
          (Ω (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) *
              (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ)
                (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) -
            U (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) *
              (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U)
                (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x))) +
        x 0 *
          (-Ω (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) *
              U (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
            (2 * cylindricalRadiusSq x *
                (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ))
                  (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
              (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ)
                (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x))) *
              (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U)
                (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) -
            2 * (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ))
                (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) *
              (U (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
                cylindricalRadiusSq x * (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] U)
                  (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)))) := by
  rw [IncompressibleFlow.vorticityStretching]
  simp only [IncompressibleFlow.convectiveDerivative_apply, Fin.sum_univ_three]
  simp only [partialDeriv_spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity_apply
    (hU.of_le (by norm_num)) hΨ, cartesianVector_apply_zero,
    ↓reduceIte, Fin.isValue, Fin.reduceEq]
  simp only [
    spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients_timeSpaceCons_apply_zero,
    spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients_timeSpaceCons_apply_one,
    spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients_timeSpaceCons_apply_two,
    spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift_timeSpaceCons,
    squaredCylindricalLift, profileSlice_apply]
  unfold cylindricalRadiusSq
  ring

/-- Second Cartesian component of vorticity stretching for independently
reconstructed swirl and azimuthal-vorticity coefficients. -/
theorem vorticityStretching_axisymmetric_apply_one
    {U Ω Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ}
    (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)
    (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ 2 Ψ)
    (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) :
    IncompressibleFlow.vorticityStretching 3
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
        (timeSpaceCons t x) 1 =
      x 0 *
          (-Ω (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) *
              (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ)
                (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
            U (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) *
              (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U)
                (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x))) +
        x 1 *
          (-Ω (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) *
              U (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
            (2 * cylindricalRadiusSq x *
                (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ))
                  (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
              (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ)
                (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x))) *
              (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U)
                (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) -
            2 * (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ))
                (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) *
              (U (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
                cylindricalRadiusSq x * (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] U)
                  (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)))) := by
  rw [IncompressibleFlow.vorticityStretching]
  simp only [IncompressibleFlow.convectiveDerivative_apply, Fin.sum_univ_three]
  simp only [partialDeriv_spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity_apply
    (hU.of_le (by norm_num)) hΨ, cartesianVector_apply_one,
    ↓reduceIte, Fin.isValue, Fin.reduceEq]
  simp only [
    spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients_timeSpaceCons_apply_zero,
    spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients_timeSpaceCons_apply_one,
    spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients_timeSpaceCons_apply_two,
    spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift_timeSpaceCons,
    squaredCylindricalLift, profileSlice_apply]
  unfold cylindricalRadiusSq
  ring

/-- Axial Cartesian component of vorticity stretching for independently
reconstructed swirl and azimuthal-vorticity coefficients. -/
theorem vorticityStretching_axisymmetric_apply_two
    {U Ω Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ}
    (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ 2 Ψ)
    (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) :
    IncompressibleFlow.vorticityStretching 3
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
        (timeSpaceCons t x) 2 =
      4 *
          ((∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ)
              (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
            cylindricalRadiusSq x *
              (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] Ψ))
                (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x))) *
          (U (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
            cylindricalRadiusSq x * (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] U)
              (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x))) -
        4 * cylindricalRadiusSq x *
          (2 * (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] Ψ)
              (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
            cylindricalRadiusSq x *
              (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] (∂[(1 : Fin 3)] Ψ))
                (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x))) *
          (∂[(2 : Fin 3)] U)
            (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) := by
  rw [IncompressibleFlow.vorticityStretching]
  simp only [IncompressibleFlow.convectiveDerivative_apply, Fin.sum_univ_three]
  have haxial : (fun xt ↦ spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ xt 2) =
      fun xt ↦ spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity (fun _ ↦ 0) Ψ xt 2 := by
    funext xt
    have h₁ := congrArg (fun v : ℝ^3 ↦ v 2)
      (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity_timeSpaceCons_eq_cartesianVector
        (hΨ.differentiable (by simp)) (U := U) (time xt) (spatialPart xt))
    have h₂ := congrArg (fun v : ℝ^3 ↦ v 2)
      (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity_timeSpaceCons_eq_cartesianVector
        (hΨ.differentiable (by simp)) (U := fun _ ↦ 0) (time xt) (spatialPart xt))
    simpa only [time, timeSpaceCons_spatialPart] using h₁.trans h₂.symm
  rw [haxial]
  simp only [partialDeriv_spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity_apply contDiff_const hΨ,
    cartesianVector_apply_two, ↓reduceIte, Fin.isValue, Fin.reduceEq]
  simp only [
    spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients_timeSpaceCons_apply_zero,
    spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients_timeSpaceCons_apply_one,
    spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients_timeSpaceCons_apply_two,
    spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift_timeSpaceCons,
    squaredCylindricalLift, profileSlice_apply]
  rw [PDE.partialDeriv_partialDeriv_comm (2 : Fin 3) (1 : Fin 3)
    (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num))
    (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x))]
  unfold cylindricalRadiusSq
  ring

/-! ## Reconstruction of the Euler vorticity residual -/

/-- The first Cartesian Euler vorticity residual is the corresponding
axisymmetric combination of the two reduced residuals. -/
theorem eulerVorticityTransportResidual_axisymmetric_apply_zero
    {U Ω Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ}
    (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)
    (hΩ : ContDiff ℝ 1 Ω)
    (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ 2 Ψ)
    (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) :
    IncompressibleFlow.vorticityTransportResidual 3 0
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
        (timeSpaceCons t x) 0 =
      -x 0 * (∂[(2 : Fin 3)]
          (squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual U Ψ))
          (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) -
        x 1 * squaredRadiusEulerVorticityResidual U Ω Ψ
          (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) := by
  rw [IncompressibleFlow.vorticityTransportResidual_zero_viscosity]
  change
    IncompressibleFlow.materialDerivative 3
          (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
          (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
          (timeSpaceCons t x) 0 -
        IncompressibleFlow.vorticityStretching 3
          (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
          (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
          (timeSpaceCons t x) 0 = _
  rw [materialDerivative_vorticityFromCoefficients_apply_zero hU hΩ hΨ,
    vorticityStretching_axisymmetric_apply_zero hU hΨ]
  rw [squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative_partialDeriv_two
    (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num))
    (hU.of_le (by norm_num))]
  rw [partialDeriv_squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual hU hΨ]
  have hu := spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity_timeSpaceCons_eq_cartesianVector
    (hΨ.differentiable (by simp)) (U := U) t x
  have hu0 := congrArg (fun v : ℝ^3 ↦ v 0) hu
  have hu1 := congrArg (fun v : ℝ^3 ↦ v 1) hu
  rw [hu0, hu1]
  simp only [cartesianVector_apply_zero, cartesianVector_apply_one,
    spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift_timeSpaceCons,
    squaredCylindricalLift, profileSlice_apply]
  unfold squaredRadiusEulerVorticityResidual
  have hq : timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x) 1 =
      cylindricalRadiusSq x := by
    change squaredCylindricalMap x 0 = cylindricalRadiusSq x
    exact squaredCylindricalMap_apply_zero x
  rw [hq]
  rw [PDE.partialDeriv_partialDeriv_comm (2 : Fin 3) (1 : Fin 3)
    (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num))
    (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x))]
  ring

/-- The second Cartesian Euler vorticity residual is the corresponding
axisymmetric combination of the two reduced residuals. -/
theorem eulerVorticityTransportResidual_axisymmetric_apply_one
    {U Ω Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ}
    (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)
    (hΩ : ContDiff ℝ 1 Ω)
    (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ 2 Ψ)
    (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) :
    IncompressibleFlow.vorticityTransportResidual 3 0
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
        (timeSpaceCons t x) 1 =
      -x 1 * (∂[(2 : Fin 3)]
          (squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual U Ψ))
          (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
        x 0 * squaredRadiusEulerVorticityResidual U Ω Ψ
          (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) := by
  rw [IncompressibleFlow.vorticityTransportResidual_zero_viscosity]
  change
    IncompressibleFlow.materialDerivative 3
          (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
          (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
          (timeSpaceCons t x) 1 -
        IncompressibleFlow.vorticityStretching 3
          (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
          (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
          (timeSpaceCons t x) 1 = _
  rw [materialDerivative_vorticityFromCoefficients_apply_one hU hΩ hΨ,
    vorticityStretching_axisymmetric_apply_one hU hΨ]
  rw [squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative_partialDeriv_two
    (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num))
    (hU.of_le (by norm_num))]
  rw [partialDeriv_squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual hU hΨ]
  have hu := spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity_timeSpaceCons_eq_cartesianVector
    (hΨ.differentiable (by simp)) (U := U) t x
  have hu0 := congrArg (fun v : ℝ^3 ↦ v 0) hu
  have hu1 := congrArg (fun v : ℝ^3 ↦ v 1) hu
  rw [hu0, hu1]
  simp only [cartesianVector_apply_zero, cartesianVector_apply_one,
    spacetimeSquaredCylindricalLift_timeSpaceCons,
    squaredCylindricalLift, profileSlice_apply]
  unfold squaredRadiusEulerVorticityResidual
  have hq : timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x) 1 =
      cylindricalRadiusSq x := by
    change squaredCylindricalMap x 0 = cylindricalRadiusSq x
    exact squaredCylindricalMap_apply_zero x
  rw [hq]
  rw [PDE.partialDeriv_partialDeriv_comm (2 : Fin 3) (1 : Fin 3)
    (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num))
    (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x))]
  ring

/-- The axial Cartesian Euler vorticity residual is the regular
squared-radius reconstruction of the swirl residual. -/
theorem eulerVorticityTransportResidual_axisymmetric_apply_two
    {U Ω Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ}
    (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)
    (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ 2 Ψ)
    (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) :
    IncompressibleFlow.vorticityTransportResidual 3 0
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
        (timeSpaceCons t x) 2 =
      2 * squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual U Ψ
          (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
        2 * cylindricalRadiusSq x * (∂[(1 : Fin 3)]
          (squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual U Ψ))
          (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) := by
  rw [IncompressibleFlow.vorticityTransportResidual_zero_viscosity]
  change
    IncompressibleFlow.materialDerivative 3
          (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
          (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
          (timeSpaceCons t x) 2 -
        IncompressibleFlow.vorticityStretching 3
          (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
          (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
          (timeSpaceCons t x) 2 = _
  rw [materialDerivative_vorticityFromCoefficients_apply_two hU hΨ,
    vorticityStretching_axisymmetric_apply_two hΨ]
  rw [squaredRadiusMaterialDerivative_partialDeriv_one
    (hΨ.of_le (by norm_num))
    (hU.of_le (by norm_num))]
  rw [partialDeriv_squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual hU hΨ]
  have hq : timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x) 1 =
      cylindricalRadiusSq x := by
    change squaredCylindricalMap x 0 = cylindricalRadiusSq x
    exact squaredCylindricalMap_apply_zero x
  rw [hq]
  unfold squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual
  ring

/-- The full Cartesian Euler vorticity residual is the division-free
reconstruction of the two reduced residuals. -/
theorem eulerVorticityTransportResidual_axisymmetric
    {U Ω Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ}
    (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)
    (hΩ : ContDiff ℝ 1 Ω)
    (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ 2 Ψ)
    (t : ℝ) (x : ℝ^3) :
    IncompressibleFlow.vorticityTransportResidual 3 0
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω)
        (timeSpaceCons t x) =
      cartesianVector
        (-x 0 * (∂[(2 : Fin 3)]
            (squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual U Ψ))
            (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) -
          x 1 * squaredRadiusEulerVorticityResidual U Ω Ψ
            (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)))
        (-x 1 * (∂[(2 : Fin 3)]
            (squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual U Ψ))
            (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
          x 0 * squaredRadiusEulerVorticityResidual U Ω Ψ
            (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)))
        (2 * squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual U Ψ
            (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x)) +
          2 * cylindricalRadiusSq x * (∂[(1 : Fin 3)]
            (squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual U Ψ))
            (timeSpaceCons t (squaredCylindricalMap x))) := by
  ext i
  fin_cases i
  · simpa using eulerVorticityTransportResidual_axisymmetric_apply_zero
      hU hΩ hΨ t x
  · simpa using eulerVorticityTransportResidual_axisymmetric_apply_one
      hU hΩ hΨ t x
  · simpa using eulerVorticityTransportResidual_axisymmetric_apply_two
      (Ω := Ω) hU hΨ t x

/-- C² swirl and streamfunction and C¹ vorticity satisfying the reduced equations give the
Cartesian transport equation for the independently reconstructed vorticity.
Identifying this field with the velocity's curl requires the reduced stream equation. -/
theorem eulerVorticityTransportResidual_axisymmetric_eq_zero
    {U Ω Ψ : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ}
    (hU : ContDiff ℝ 2 U)
    (hΩ : ContDiff ℝ 1 Ω)
    (hΨ : ContDiff ℝ 2 Ψ)
    (hSwirl : squaredRadiusEulerSwirlResidual U Ψ = 0)
    (hVorticity : squaredRadiusEulerVorticityResidual U Ω Ψ = 0) :
    IncompressibleFlow.vorticityTransportResidual 3 0
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVelocity U Ψ)
        (spacetimeAxisymmetricVorticityFromCoefficients U Ω) = 0 := by
  funext xt
  rw [← timeSpaceCons_spatialPart xt]
  rw [eulerVorticityTransportResidual_axisymmetric hU hΩ hΨ]
  rw [hSwirl, hVorticity]
  have hzero (i : Fin 3) (q : SpaceTime 2) :
      (∂[i] (0 : SpaceTime 2 → ℝ)) q = 0 := by
    change (∂[i] (fun _ : SpaceTime 2 ↦ (0 : ℝ))) q = 0
    exact PDE.partialDeriv_const 0
  ext i
  fin_cases i <;> simp [hzero]

end

end AxisymmetricFlow
